{"pyq_id": "JEEM-2026-04-02-S1-Q48", "exam": "JEE_MAIN", "year": 2026, "shift": "02 Apr S1", "subject": "PHYSICS", "chapter": "Moving Charges and Magnetism", "topic": "Lorentz force", "question_format": "numerical_integer", "stem": "1 μC charge moving with velocity v = (î − 2ĵ + 3k̂) m/s in the region of magnetic field B = (2î + 3ĵ − 5k̂) T. The magnitude of force acting on it is √α × 10^−6 N. The value of α is ____.", "options": [], "answer_key": "171", "key_source": "unofficial_reference", "source": {"document": "JEE Main 2026 02-Apr Shift-1 (eSaral reproduction).pdf", "rights_status": "UNKNOWN", "permitted_uses": ["storage", "search"], "page": 4}, "extraction": {"method": "manual", "visual_review_done": true}, "formal": {"kind": "equation_system", "knowns": {"q": {"value": "1", "unit": "uC"}, "vx": {"value": "1", "unit": "m/s"}, "vy": {"value": "-2", "unit": "m/s"}, "vz": {"value": "3", "unit": "m/s"}, "Bx": {"value": "2", "unit": "T"}, "By": {"value": "3", "unit": "T"}, "Bz": {"value": "-5", "unit": "T"}, "u": {"value": "1", "unit": "uN"}}, "unknowns": {"Fx": {"unit": "N", "domain": "real"}, "Fy": {"unit": "N", "domain": "real"}, "Fz": {"unit": "N", "domain": "real"}, "F": {"unit": "N", "domain": "positive"}, "al": {"unit": "", "domain": "positive"}}, "equations": ["Fx = q*(vy*Bz - vz*By)", "Fy = q*(vz*Bx - vx*Bz)", "Fz = q*(vx*By - vy*Bx)", "F**2 = Fx**2 + Fy**2 + Fz**2", "F = sqrt(al)*u"], "target": "al", "model": ["F = q v x B, components of the cross product"]}, "numerical_rounding": "nearest_integer"}
{"pyq_id": "JEEM-2026-04-02-S1-Q49", "exam": "JEE_MAIN", "year": 2026, "shift": "02 Apr S1", "subject": "PHYSICS", "chapter": "Mechanical Properties of Solids", "topic": "stress in a hanging wire", "question_format": "numerical_integer", "stem": "A uniform wire of length l of weight w is suspended from the roof with a weight of W at the other end. The stress in the wire at l/3 distance from the top is (W/A + 2w/(γA)), where A is the cross sectional area of the wire. The value of γ is ____.", "options": [], "answer_key": "3", "key_source": "unofficial_reference", "source": {"document": "JEE Main 2026 02-Apr Shift-1 (eSaral reproduction).pdf", "rights_status": "UNKNOWN", "permitted_uses": ["storage", "search"], "page": 4}, "extraction": {"method": "manual", "visual_review_done": true}, "formal": {"kind": "equation_system", "knowns": {"W": {"value": "symbolic", "unit": "N"}, "w": {"value": "symbolic", "unit": "N"}, "A": {"value": "symbolic", "unit": "m^2"}}, "unknowns": {"T": {"unit": "N", "domain": "positive"}, "g": {"unit": "", "domain": "positive"}}, "equations": ["T = W + w*(2/3)", "T/A = W/A + 2*w/(g*A)"], "target": "g", "model": ["tension at l/3 from top supports W and the 2l/3 of wire below"]}, "numerical_rounding": "nearest_integer"}
{"pyq_id": "JEEM-2026-04-02-S1-Q50", "exam": "JEE_MAIN", "year": 2026, "shift": "02 Apr S1", "subject": "PHYSICS", "chapter": "Mechanical Properties of Fluids", "topic": "flotation", "question_format": "numerical_integer", "stem": "A tub is filled with water and a wooden cube 10 cm × 10 cm × 10 cm is placed in the water. The wooden cube is found to float on the water with a part of it submerged in water. When a metal coin is placed on the wooden cube, the submerged part is increased by 3.87 cm. The mass of the metal coin is ____ gram. (Take water density as 1 g/cm^3 and density of wood as 0.4 g/cm^3)", "options": [], "answer_key": "387", "key_source": "unofficial_reference", "source": {"document": "JEE Main 2026 02-Apr Shift-1 (eSaral reproduction).pdf", "rights_status": "UNKNOWN", "permitted_uses": ["storage", "search"], "page": 4}, "extraction": {"method": "manual", "visual_review_done": true}, "formal": {"kind": "equation_system", "knowns": {"rho": {"value": "1", "unit": "g/cm^3"}, "s": {"value": "10", "unit": "cm"}, "dh": {"value": "3.87", "unit": "cm"}, "gr": {"value": "symbolic", "unit": "m/s^2"}}, "unknowns": {"mc": {"unit": "g", "domain": "positive"}}, "equations": ["mc*gr = rho*s**2*dh*gr"], "target": "mc", "model": ["coin weight = extra buoyancy; cube does not sink fully (4 + 3.87 < 10 cm)"]}, "numerical_rounding": "nearest_integer"}
{"pyq_id": "JEEM-2026-04-02-S1-Q51", "exam": "JEE_MAIN", "year": 2026, "shift": "02 Apr S1", "subject": "CHEMISTRY", "chapter": "Some Basic Concepts", "topic": "stoichiometry", "question_format": "single_correct_mcq", "stem": "The mass of iron converted into Fe3O4 by the action of 18 g of steam is: (Given: Molar mass of H, O and Fe are 1, 16 and 56 g mol^−1 respectively) Assume iron is present in excess:", "options": [{"id": "A", "text": "2.1 g", "value": "2.1"}, {"id": "B", "text": "4.2 g", "value": "4.2"}, {"id": "C", "text": "21 g", "value": "21"}, {"id": "D", "text": "42 g", "value": "42"}], "answer_key": "D", "key_source": "unofficial_reference", "source": {"document": "JEE Main 2026 02-Apr Shift-1 (eSaral reproduction).pdf", "rights_status": "UNKNOWN", "permitted_uses": ["storage", "search"], "page": 4}, "extraction": {"method": "manual", "visual_review_done": true}, "formal": {"kind": "stoichiometry", "reaction": "3 Fe + 4 H2O -> Fe3O4 + 4 H2", "given": {"H2O": {"mass_g": "18"}}, "atomic_masses": {"H": "1", "O": "16", "Fe": "56"}, "target": {"species": "Fe", "quantity": "mass_g"}, "reaction_source": "standard: 3Fe + 4H2O(g) -> Fe3O4 + 4H2 (equation not printed in the stem)"}}
{"pyq_id": "JEEM-2026-04-02-S1-Q52", "exam": "JEE_MAIN", "year": 2026, "shift": "02 Apr S1", "subject": "CHEMISTRY", "chapter": "Structure of Atom", "topic": "ionisation energy of H-like ion", "question_format": "single_correct_mcq", "stem": "What is the energy (in J atom^−1) required for the following process? Li^2+(g) → Li^3+(g) + e^−. (Take the ionization energy for the H atom in the ground state as 2.18 × 10^−18 J atom^−1)", "options": [{"id": "A", "text": "8.72 × 10^−18", "value": "8.72*10**-18"}, {"id": "B", "text": "1.962 × 10^−18", "value": "1.962*10**-18"}, {"id": "C", "text": "1.962 × 10^−17", "value": "1.962*10**-17"}, {"id": "D", "text": "6.54 × 10^−17", "value": "6.54*10**-17"}], "answer_key": "C", "key_source": "unofficial_reference", "source": {"document": "JEE Main 2026 02-Apr Shift-1 (eSaral reproduction).pdf", "rights_status": "UNKNOWN", "permitted_uses": ["storage", "search"], "page": 4}, "extraction": {"method": "manual", "visual_review_done": true}, "formal": {"kind": "equation_system", "knowns": {"EH": {"value": "2.18*10**-18", "unit": "J"}, "Z": {"value": "3", "unit": ""}}, "unknowns": {"E": {"unit": "J", "domain": "positive"}}, "equations": ["E = Z**2*EH"], "target": "E", "model": ["hydrogen-like ion ground state: IE = Z^2 x IE(H)"]}}
{"pyq_id": "JEEM-2026-04-02-S1-Q54", "exam": "JEE_MAIN", "year": 2026, "shift": "02 Apr S1", "subject": "CHEMISTRY", "chapter": "Thermodynamics", "topic": "Hess's law", "question_format": "single_correct_mcq", "stem": "Consider the following data. (i) 2Al(s) + 6HCl(aq) → Al2Cl6(aq) + 3H2(g) + 1200 kJ/mol (ii) H2(g) + Cl2(g) → 2HCl(g) + 164 kJ/mol. (iii) HCl(g) + aq → HCl(aq) + 83 kJ/mol. (iv) Al2Cl6(s) + aq → Al2Cl6(aq) + 663 kJ/mol. The enthalpy of formation of anhydrous solid Al2Cl6 is:", "options": [{"id": "A", "text": "−648 kJ mol^−1", "value": "-648"}, {"id": "B", "text": "−1350 kJ mol^−1", "value": "-1350"}, {"id": "C", "text": "−2002 kJ mol^−1", "value": "-2002"}, {"id": "D", "text": "−1527 kJ mol^−1", "value": "-1527"}], "answer_key": "D", "key_source": "unofficial_reference", "source": {"document": "JEE Main 2026 02-Apr Shift-1 (eSaral reproduction).pdf", "rights_status": "UNKNOWN", "permitted_uses": ["storage", "search"], "page": 5}, "extraction": {"method": "manual", "visual_review_done": true}, "formal": {"kind": "equation_system", "knowns": {"H1": {"value": "-1200", "unit": "kJ/mol"}, "H2": {"value": "-164", "unit": "kJ/mol"}, "H3": {"value": "-83", "unit": "kJ/mol"}, "H4": {"value": "-663", "unit": "kJ/mol"}}, "unknowns": {"Hf": {"unit": "kJ/mol", "domain": "real"}}, "equations": ["Hf = H1 + 3*H2 + 6*H3 - H4"], "target": "Hf", "model": ["heat written on the product side = exothermic (negative dH)", "target 2Al + 3Cl2 -> Al2Cl6(s) = (i) + 3(ii) + 6(iii) - (iv)"]}}
{"pyq_id": "JEEM-2026-04-02-S1-Q55", "exam": "JEE_MAIN", "year": 2026, "shift": "02 Apr S1", "subject": "CHEMISTRY", "chapter": "Solutions", "topic": "colligative property and Ka", "question_format": "single_correct_mcq", "stem": "19.5 g of fluoro acetic acid (molar mass = 78 g mol^−1) is dissolved in 500 g of water at 298 K. The depression in the freezing point of water was 1°C. What is Ka of fluoro acetic acid? (For water, Kf = 1.86 K kg mol^−1). Assume molarity and molality to have same values.", "options": [{"id": "A", "text": "10^−6", "value": "10**-6"}, {"id": "B", "text": "4 × 10^−4", "value": "4*10**-4"}, {"id": "C", "text": "3 × 10^−5", "value": "3*10**-5"}, {"id": "D", "text": "3 × 10^−3", "value": "3*10**-3"}], "answer_key": "D", "key_source": "unofficial_reference", "source": {"document": "JEE Main 2026 02-Apr Shift-1 (eSaral reproduction).pdf", "rights_status": "UNKNOWN", "permitted_uses": ["storage", "search"], "page": 5}, "extraction": {"method": "manual", "visual_review_done": true}, "formal": {"kind": "equation_system", "options_rounded": {"rel_tol": "0.05"}, "knowns": {"w": {"value": "19.5", "unit": "g"}, "M": {"value": "78", "unit": "g/mol"}, "W": {"value": "500", "unit": "g"}, "Kf": {"value": "1.86", "unit": "K*kg/mol"}, "dT": {"value": "1", "unit": "K"}}, "unknowns": {"m": {"unit": "mol/kg", "domain": "positive"}, "i": {"unit": "", "domain": "positive"}, "a": {"unit": "", "domain": "positive"}, "Ka": {"unit": "mol/kg", "domain": "positive"}}, "equations": ["m*M*W = w", "dT = i*Kf*m", "i = 1 + a", "Ka*(1 - a) = m*a**2"], "target": "Ka", "model": ["HA <=> H+ + A-: i = 1 + alpha", "Ka = c alpha^2/(1 - alpha) with c = molality"]}}
{"pyq_id": "JEEM-2026-04-02-S1-Q71", "exam": "JEE_MAIN", "year": 2026, "shift": "02 Apr S1", "subject": "CHEMISTRY", "chapter": "Coordination Compounds", "topic": "ionisation isomer test", "question_format": "numerical_integer", "stem": "5.33 g of CrCl3·6H2O, which is a 1 : 3 electrolyte, is dissolved in water and is passed through a cation exchanger. The chloride ions in the eluted solution, on treatment with AgNO3 results in 8.61 g of AgCl. The ratio of moles of complex reacted and moles of AgCl formed is ____ × 10^−2. (Nearest integer) [Molar mass in g mol^−1 Cr : 52, Ag : 108, Cl : 35.5, H : 1, O : 16]", "options": [], "answer_key": "33", "key_source": "unofficial_reference", "source": {"document": "JEE Main 2026 02-Apr Shift-1 (eSaral reproduction).pdf", "rights_status": "UNKNOWN", "permitted_uses": ["storage", "search"], "page": 7}, "extraction": {"method": "manual", "visual_review_done": true}, "formal": {"kind": "equation_system", "knowns": {"m1": {"value": "5.33", "unit": "g"}, "m2": {"value": "8.61", "unit": "g"}, "MCr": {"value": "52", "unit": "g/mol"}, "MCl": {"value": "35.5", "unit": "g/mol"}, "MH": {"value": "1", "unit": "g/mol"}, "MO": {"value": "16", "unit": "g/mol"}, "MAg": {"value": "108", "unit": "g/mol"}}, "unknowns": {"Mc": {"unit": "g/mol", "domain": "positive"}, "Ma": {"unit": "g/mol", "domain": "positive"}, "n1": {"unit": "mol", "domain": "positive"}, "n2": {"unit": "mol", "domain": "positive"}, "x": {"unit": "", "domain": "positive"}}, "equations": ["Mc = MCr + 3*MCl + 6*(2*MH + MO)", "Ma = MAg + MCl", "n1*Mc = m1", "n2*Ma = m2", "x/100 = n1/n2"], "target": "x", "model": ["moles from given masses; the 1:3 information is not needed for the asked ratio"]}, "numerical_rounding": "nearest_integer"}
{"pyq_id": "JEEM-2026-04-02-S1-Q73", "exam": "JEE_MAIN", "year": 2026, "shift": "02 Apr S1", "subject": "CHEMISTRY", "chapter": "Hydrocarbons", "topic": "combustion of alkane", "question_format": "numerical_integer", "stem": "One mole of an alkane (x) requires 8 mole oxygen for complete combustion. Sum of number of carbon and hydrogen atoms in the alkane (x) is ____.", "options": [], "answer_key": "17", "key_source": "unofficial_reference", "source": {"document": "JEE Main 2026 02-Apr Shift-1 (eSaral reproduction).pdf", "rights_status": "UNKNOWN", "permitted_uses": ["storage", "search"], "page": 7}, "extraction": {"method": "manual", "visual_review_done": true}, "formal": {"kind": "equation_system", "knowns": {}, "unknowns": {"n": {"unit": "", "domain": "natural"}, "s": {"unit": "", "domain": "natural"}}, "equations": ["(3*n + 1)/2 = 8", "s = n + (2*n + 2)"], "target": "s", "model": ["CnH2n+2 + (3n+1)/2 O2 -> n CO2 + (n+1) H2O"]}, "numerical_rounding": "nearest_integer"}
{"pyq_id": "JEEM-2026-04-02-S1-Q74", "exam": "JEE_MAIN", "year": 2026, "shift": "02 Apr S1", "subject": "CHEMISTRY", "chapter": "Chemical Kinetics", "topic": "Arrhenius equation", "question_format": "numerical_integer", "stem": "For reaction A → P, rate constant k = 1.5 × 10^3 s^−1 at 27°C. If activation energy for the above reaction is 60 kJ mol^−1, then the temperature (in °C) at which rate constant, k = 4.5 × 10^3 s^−1 is ____. (Nearest integer) Given: log 2 = 0.30, log 3 = 0.48, R = 8.3 J K^−1 mol^−1, ln 10 = 2.3", "options": [], "answer_key": "41", "key_source": "unofficial_reference", "source": {"document": "JEE Main 2026 02-Apr Shift-1 (eSaral reproduction).pdf", "rights_status": "UNKNOWN", "permitted_uses": ["storage", "search"], "page": 7}, "extraction": {"method": "manual", "visual_review_done": true}, "formal": {"kind": "equation_system", "knowns": {"Ea": {"value": "60", "unit": "kJ/mol"}, "R": {"value": "8.3", "unit": "J/(mol*K)"}, "T1": {"value": "300", "unit": "K"}, "L3": {"value": "2.3*0.48", "unit": ""}, "K1": {"value": "1", "unit": "K"}}, "unknowns": {"T2": {"unit": "K", "domain": "positive"}, "tc": {"unit": "", "domain": "real"}}, "equations": ["L3 = (Ea/R)*(1/T1 - 1/T2)", "tc = T2/K1 - 273"], "target": "tc", "model": ["ln(k2/k1) = ln 3 = 2.3 x 0.48 (given values)", "27 C = 300 K; C = K - 273 (as given data implies)"]}, "numerical_rounding": "nearest_integer"}
{"pyq_id": "JEEM-2026-04-02-S1-Q75", "exam": "JEE_MAIN", "year": 2026, "shift": "02 Apr S1", "subject": "CHEMISTRY", "chapter": "Thermodynamics", "topic": "transition temperature", "question_format": "numerical_integer", "stem": "At the transition temperature T, A ⇌ B and ΔG° = 105 − 35 log T where A and B are two states of substance X. The transition temperature in °C when pressure is 1 atm is ____. (Nearest integer)", "options": [], "answer_key": "727", "key_source": "unofficial_reference", "source": {"document": "JEE Main 2026 02-Apr Shift-1 (eSaral reproduction).pdf", "rights_status": "UNKNOWN", "permitted_uses": ["storage", "search"], "page": 7}, "extraction": {"method": "manual", "visual_review_done": true}, "formal": {"kind": "equation_system", "knowns": {}, "unknowns": {"T": {"unit": "", "domain": "positive"}, "tc": {"unit": "", "domain": "real"}}, "equations": ["105 - 35*log(T, 10) = 0", "tc = T - 273"], "target": "tc", "model": ["at transition dG = 0 (equilibrium at 1 atm)", "log = log10; T in K as a pure number"]}, "numerical_rounding": "nearest_integer"}
